        "created_at": "2021-07-10T04:35:42.201Z",
        "cooked": "<p>i know there is an example in the book with Jen and Maggie rolling an extra die for a “hit the deck” twist but should we normally consider the single die rolled as a reaction as min, mid, and max?</p>\n<p>My specific action sequence<br>\nYellow- Strength in Victory<br>\nRed- Push your limits<br>\nRed- Reactive strike</p>\n<p>being swarmed by minions while in the red zone<br>\nI get hit<br>\nreact attack killing the minion<br>\n1damage react to heal based on min die<br>\nsecond minion attacks<br>\n1damage react kill minion<br>\n1damage react heal min die<br>\nthird minion 2 damage kill and heal</p>\n<p>relooking at my players character sheet Strength in Victory uses a different power/quality than Reactive Strike so it will not come up but it is still a legal combo so i will finish asking my question</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-07-10T04:35:42.201Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
